WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.095
Express and other Node.js frameworks make it easy to receive request data,

00:00:04.095 --> 00:00:06.995
but they do not automatically know the application's rules.

00:00:06.995 --> 00:00:10.450
Request bodies, path parameters, query parameters, headers, cookies,

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:13.035
and file metadata all need explicit expectations.

00:00:13.035 --> 00:00:15.050
Middleware can help centralize validation,

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.187
but each route should still have a clear contract for what it accepts.

00:00:18.187 --> 00:00:21.000
Frontend form validation should align with server validation.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.740
A form might enforce required fields, length, and format for usability,

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.660
while the API enforces the same rules authoritatively.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.495
When frontend and backend rules diverge,

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:33.850
users get confusing errors and attackers get opportunities to submit data the server did

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.920
not expect. Shared schema patterns can help reduce that drift.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.960
URL and route parameters need context.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.840
A value that looks like an identifier may still need to match the authenticated user's

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:43.953
tenant or permissions.

00:00:43.953 --> 00:00:48.480
Headers and cookies may require format checks, signature verification, expiration checks,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:49.480
and safe parsing.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:53.640
Uploaded files need validation of size, name, declared type, detected content,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.200
storage location, and later access behavior.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:00.200
GraphQL and WebSocket inputs deserve the same care as REST APIs.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.035
GraphQL schemas describe operations,

00:01:02.035 --> 00:01:04.920
but authorization and business rules still need enforcement.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.900
WebSocket messages are long-lived external input and should be parsed, typed,

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.515
size-limited, and validated by message type.

00:01:11.515 --> 00:01:13.720
Every protocol boundary is a validation boundary.
